ities, and clinical outcomes. CNS Spectr 2000;5:55–65. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 17. Baxter JD, Young WF, Jr, Webb P. Cardiovascular endocrinology: introduction. Endocr Rev 2003;24:253–60. 10.1210/er.2003-0099 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 18. Libby P. Inflammation in atherosclerosis. Nature 2002;420:868–74. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 19. Stier CT, Jr, Chander PN, Rocha R. Aldosterone as a mediator in cardiovascular injury. Cardiol Rev 2002;10:97–107. 10.1097/00045415-200203000-00008 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 20. Rossi E, Regolisti G, Negro A. et al High prevalence of primary aldosteronism using post-captopril plasma aldosterone to renin ratio as a screening test among Italian hypertensives. Am J Hypertens 2002;15:896–902. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 21. Young WF., Jr Primary aldosteronism: a common and curable form of hypertension. Cardiol Rev 1999;7:207–14 [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 22. Golub MS. The adrenal and the metabolic syndrome. Curr Hypertens Rep 2001;3:117–20. 10.1007/s11906-001-0022-x [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 23. Baxter JD. Advances in glucocorticoid therapy. Adv Intern Med 2000;45:317–49. [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 24. Bain J. The many faces of testosterone. Clin Interv Aging 2007;2:567–76. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 25. Kuller LH. Hormone replacement therapy and risk of cardiovascular disease: implications of the results of the Women''s Health Initiative. Arterioscler Thromb Vasc Biol 2003;23:11–6. 10.1161/01.ATV.0000046033.32478.6D [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 26. Grant P. A new approach to diabetic control: fuzzy logic and insulin pump technology. Med Eng Phys 2007;29:824–7. 10.1016/j.medengphy.2006.08.014 [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 27. Srinivasan P, Huang GC, Amiel SA, Heaton ND. Islet cell transplantation. Postgrad Med J 2007;83:224–9. 10.1136/pgmj.2006.053447 [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 28. Volt