DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 194. Foti P. V., Attinà G., Spadola S., et al., “MR Imaging of Ovarian Masses: Classification and Differential Diagnosis,” Insights into Imaging 7, no. 1 (2016): 21–41. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 195. Sarfati J., Bachelot A., Coussieu C., Meduri G., and Touraine P., “Impact of Clinical, Hormonal, Radiological, and Immunohistochemical Studies on the Diagnosis of Postmenopausal Hyperandrogenism,” European Journal of Endocrinology 165, no. 5 (2011): 779–788. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 196. Iyer V. R. and Lee S. I., “MRI, CT, and PET/CT for Ovarian Cancer Detection and Adnexal Lesion Characterization,” American Journal of Roentgenology 194, no. 2 (2010): 311–321. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 197. Liu Y., Zhang H., Li X., and Qi G., “Combined Application of Ultrasound and CT Increased Diagnostic Value in Female Patients With Pelvic Masses,” Computational and Mathematical Methods in Medicine 2016 (2016): 1–5. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 198. McCarthy‐Keith D. M., Hill M., Norian J. M., Millo C., McKeeby J., and Armstrong A. Y., “Use of F 18‐fluoro‐D‐glucose‐Positron Emission Tomography‐Computed Tomography to Localize a Hilar Cell Tumor of the Ovary,” Fertility and Sterility 94, no. 2 (2010): 753.e11–753.e14. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 199. Prassopoulos V., Laspas F., Vlachou F., Efthimiadou R., Gogou L., and Andreou J., “Leydig Cell Tumour of the Ovary Localised With Positron Emission Tomography/Computed Tomography,” Gynecological Endocrinology 27, no. 10 (2011): 837–839. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 200. Wong F. C. K., Chan A. Z., Wong W. S., et al., “Hyperandrogenism, Elevated 17‐Hydroxyprogesterone and Its Urinary Metabolites in a Young Woman With Ovarian Steroid Cell Tumor, Not Otherwise Specified: Case Report and Review of the Literature,” Case Reports in Endocrinology 2019 (October 2019): 9237459. [ DOI ] [ P